  "analysis": {
    "summary": "A falling {{chord 1}} arpeggio ends on its b7, which drops a half step to the 3rd of the dominant. The chart's plain V7 is played here as {{chord 2}}, the usual Gypsy-jazz reading of the dominant in a minor key: a quick triplet sweeps up a diminished 7th arpeggio from its 3rd to the b9. The b9 is held, then falls a half step to the 5th of {{chord 3}}, and the line walks down the minor 6 arpeggio to finish on the 6th.",
